  "query_preview": "..Drier air has moved into Arizona with PWAT values\ndropping around 0.25\" and dewpoints dropping 15-20 degrees\ncompared to 24 hours ago. Expect further drying as broad high\npressure sets up over the region centered over Sonora. High\ntemperatures will be right around normal through the weekend\nthen warm to a few degrees above normal starting Monday as the\nridge nudges a little further north and becomes centered over\nsouthern Arizona. Winds will be gusty out of the west/northwest \neach afternoon due to daytime momentum transfer with the strongest\nwinds expected in Graham and Greenlee Counties.",
